WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:06.010
Let's debate whether children kept in cages
deserve things like beds and toothbrushes

00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:07.390
and soap.

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:12.920
This is how far the Overton window has moved
on the issue of child detentions and separations

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:14.019
and incarcerations.

00:00:14.019 --> 00:00:20.080
Uh, or to put it in another way, this is how
much creeping normality there has been on

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.330
the issue of caging children.

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:25.480
So let me explain those two terms because
these are important.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:29.260
When I talk about the Overton window and I
say the Overton window has shifted on this

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:33.440
issue, the Overton window is the range of
what's acceptable for debate in the public

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:34.440
discourse.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:35.440
Okay?

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:41.520
So, for example, in the area of nuclear weapons,
the Overton window, more or less ranges from

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:44.800
everybody who wants a new car should have
nukes or everyone should have knew sort of

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:47.930
on one side two, no one should have nukes.

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:53.011
Uh, and there should or shouldn't be international
agreements limiting who has nukes and there

00:00:53.011 --> 00:00:58.360
should or shouldn't be punishments like international
sanctions for people for country's that violate

00:00:58.360 --> 00:00:59.570
agreements on new cars.

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:00.570
Okay.

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:04.270
That's sort of all within the Overton window
on nuclear weapons outside of the Overton

00:01:04.270 --> 00:01:08.820
window right now would be the position that
if a country develops nuclear weapons when

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:14.289
they shouldn't we capture torture and kill
the children of whoever is president or prime

00:01:14.289 --> 00:01:15.289
minister at the time.

00:01:15.289 --> 00:01:16.289
All right.

00:01:16.289 --> 00:01:20.890
That's a cartoonish example, but that is a
piece of position on nuclear weapons that

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:23.040
is outside of the Overton window right now.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.040
It's not.

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:27.950
When you hear that, you don't consider that
to be part of what is the acceptable a spectrum

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:30.670
of debate or position on nuclear weapons.

00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:32.439
That's Overton window creeping.

00:01:32.439 --> 00:01:36.380
Normality is another term where you can't
jump to where we are today.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:38.499
It has to creep in slowly.

00:01:38.499 --> 00:01:39.499
Normalizing.

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:44.689
So as an example, if 20 years ago someone
had said, let's radicalize half the country

00:01:44.689 --> 00:01:49.109
on immigration so that they think Brown people
from Latin America are the enemy who are tape

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:51.500
taking our jobs and raping us.

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:56.289
And then let's start putting children who
come here with undocumented parents in cages

00:01:56.289 --> 00:02:01.639
and we only have to debate do those kids deserve
soap and beds and toothbrushes?

00:02:01.639 --> 00:02:03.170
That would be too much.

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:05.989
But that creeps in over 20 years.

00:02:05.989 --> 00:02:12.069
And here we are debating, do children in the
